Notebook[{
Cell["ExtendInfraSegment", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"37692e0a-8c9d-4a2f-a437-ba320a430998"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"57c721de-00cc-47ab-9aaa-144f652f46d1"],

Cell["\<\
ExtendInfraSegment[graph, a, b, c, d] returns InfraPoint[{x}] for x with B(a, \
b, x) and d(b, x) == d(c, d) (Tarski axiom A4 synthetic-extension). \
ExtendInfraSegment[graph, a, b, c, d, n] / UpTo[n] / All controls \
multiplicity. The 2-arg ExtendInfraSegment[graph, segment] form (extend \
segment to a maximal line) has been removed; use FindInfraLine[graph, \
segment] for the geodesic case or ExtendInfraPath[graph, segment, All, \
Properties -> {\"Simple\", {\"ShortestPath\"}}] for per-step extension.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe03b933-5978-4955-9b3d-e388a5d436da"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"48a91d28-acad-4037-93ec-86807ca3e108"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"a23b3a6d-19d0-4e39-878a-7887d5eb7920"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"eddac3b4-bae7-49d0-9848-3e6d3e2c2f06"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"13e9433b-eaeb-47ab-886d-6e7696c652ee"],

